SeaVGABIOS (when built into this directory)
===========================================

Upstream project: SeaVGABIOS — the VGA BIOS option ROM built from the
                  `vgasrc/` tree of SeaBIOS (not a separate repository)
Canonical docs:   https://www.seabios.org/SeaVGABIOS
Source mirror:    https://gitlab.com/qemu-project/seabios.git
Pinned release:   rel-1.16.3 (see ../manifests/seavgabios.json)

License: GNU Lesser General Public License v3.0 or later (LGPL-3.0-or-later).
Upstream `vgasrc/` file headers read "This file may be distributed under the
terms of the GNU LGPLv3 license" and carry two copyright lines:

    Copyright (C) 2009-2013  Kevin O'Connor <kevin@koconnor.net>
    Copyright (C) 2001-2008 the LGPL VGABios developers Team

So the ROM descends from the older LGPL VGABios project as well as SeaBIOS.
The full upstream license text is copied beside vgabios.bin as
COPYING.SeaVGABIOS when you run ../build-scripts/build-seavgabios.sh.

Build configuration
-------------------
The pinned build selects the plain 256 KB standard VGA target with no SVGA
extensions, no VBE, and no PCI ROM header:

    CONFIG_QEMU=y
    CONFIG_VGA_STANDARD_VGA=y
    CONFIG_VGA_VBE=n
    CONFIG_VGA_PCI=n

VBE and the PCI ROM header are disabled because this emulator implements
neither; a ROM must not advertise a capability the machine does not have.

x86WASM project policy
----------------------
- Keep SeaVGABIOS sources and binaries under firmware/ only.
- Do not vendor SeaVGABIOS (or other LGPL/GPL firmware) sources into
  MIT/Apache Rust crates (firmware-interface, machine-pc, devices, …).
- Do not commit vgabios.bin until licensing review explicitly allows it
  (*.bin under this tree is gitignored).
- Building the ROM here does not imply SeaBIOS POST. Mapping and host-driven
  entry invoke are separate machine helpers; there is still no SeaBIOS option-
  ROM scan or INT 10h. See docs/firmware-r7-seavgabios-build.md.

See also: docs/licensing.md, docs/adr/0004-firmware-seabios-ovmf.md,
third_party/NOTICE, firmware/README.md.
